guide forever/horde/40-50/04-tanaris
title Tanaris & Searing Gorge
faction Horde
levels 45-48
zone Tanaris
next forever/horde/40-50/05-the-hinterlands
# Route from the Polestar route simulator's Horde consensus (Tauren export),
# visits 44-48, levels 45.9-47.6. Checked by lint, not play-tested on
# Forever yet. Era + known Forever quests only.
#
# Flow: Camp Mojache (where the previous guide ends) -> fly Gadgetzan
# (bind) -> Sandsorrow Watch -> Gadgetzan -> Caliph Scorpidsting -> Marvon
# Rivetseeker -> the Noxious Lair -> Dunemaul Compound -> Thistleshrub
# Valley -> Tooga's escort to Steamwheedle Port -> Gadgetzan -> Marvon ->
# Scrimshank's gear (OOX-17/TN if you found its beacon) -> hearth Gadgetzan
# -> (Hunters and Shamans: fly Orgrimmar to train; Druids: Thunder Bluff) ->
# fly Ratchet -> boat to Booty Bay -> fly Kargath -> the Grimesilt Dig
# Site -> Thorium Point (flight path) -> Kalaran Windblade and the Cauldron
# -> the Slag Pit -> the lava spiders -> the Lookouts -> Thorium Point,
# where the next guide flies on to Stonard.
#
# Deviations from the export:
# - Tanaris: Sandsorrow Watch first, so Noxious Lair Investigation (82) is
#   in hand for the western loop; Marvon's Gahz'ridian ornaments are dug up
#   on that loop and handed in on the second trip south, with Scrimshank's
#   gear. Tooga is walked straight from Thistleshrub Valley to Steamwheedle
#   Port, where Screecher Spirits (3520) is handed in too.
# - The Blasted Lands pass (visit 45, Threat From the Sea) is gone: the
#   previous guide finishes that chain at Misty Reed Post.
# - The Badlands loop (visit 47) is dropped: a long ride from Kargath to
#   the far south-west for Broken Alliances (782, 3,600 XP) and to the far
#   north for Reclaimed Treasures (2342, no longer accepted on this route).
#   The Kargath bind and both hearths to Kargath go with it.
# - Caught! (4449) is taken, done and handed in on the way into the gorge
#   from Kargath, instead of being carried through the whole zone; Thorium
#   Point's flight path then replaces the hearth out.
# - Gadgetzan on arrival: Tran'rek and the poster beside the wind rider
#   master first, then Andi Lynn, the inn and Marin; Fizzledowser on the west
#   side last, on the way out.
#
# Optional: Find and Rescue OOX-17/TN! (351, 648): the beacon is a rare
# drop; the reward waits with Oglethorpe in Booty Bay. The Key to Freedom
# (4451): the key is a rare drop.
#
# Accepted here, finished later on the route: Sprinkle's Secret Ingredient
# (2641: the Violet Tragan grows in the Hinterlands), Rise of the Silithid
# (32, Orgrimmar around 50).
#
# Class training: Hunters and Shamans fly from Gadgetzan to Orgrimmar, and
# Druids to Thunder Bluff, at about 47, before Ratchet: the next training
# stop, in the Undercity, has no trainer for them. Everyone else trains in
# the Undercity in the next guide.
#
# Left out: Into the Field (243: no longer accepted on this route), Ledger
# from Tanaris (4450: the export never hands it in), Broken Alliances (782),
# see above.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Gadgetzan

step Fly to Gadgetzan
  zone Feralas
  tip From Camp Mojache's flight master.
  fly "Gadgetzan"

step Gadgetzan
  zone Tanaris
  accept 3362                           -- Tran'rek, beside the wind rider master
  accept 2781 object 150075             -- the Wanted Poster in the square
  accept 5863                           -- Andi Lynn
  sethome "Gadgetzan" npc 7733          -- Innkeeper Fizzgrimble
  accept 2605                           -- Marin Noggenfogger
  accept 992                            -- Senior Surveyor Fizzledowser

step Sandsorrow Watch
  tip West of Gadgetzan, use the Untapped Dowsing Widget beside the water hole in the troll camp.
  collect 8585 quest 992.1 @39.0,29.2

step Gadgetzan
  turnin 992                            -- Senior Surveyor Fizzledowser
  accept 82

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- The southern loop

step Caliph Scorpidsting
  tip South-east of Gadgetzan the Wastewander bandits camp in the dunes; Caliph stands in the eastern camp.
  collect 8723 quest 2781.1 @61.8,38.2

step Marvon Rivetseeker
  tip West along the road south; Marvon camps by the ruins at the Broken Pillar. Put on his Gahz'ridian Detector: it shows the buried ornaments, here and around the Dunemaul Compound.
  accept 3161

step The Noxious Lair
  tip West, the Centipaar insects swarm around their hives; any of them drops the parts.
  collect 8587 quest 82.1

step Dunemaul Compound
  tip South of the Noxious Lair the Dunemaul ogres hold their compound, with Gor'marok the Ravager at its eastern end. Dig up Gahz'ridian ornaments between the fights.
  kill 5474 quest 5863.1
  kill 5472 quest 5863.2
  kill 12046 quest 5863.3 @41.5,57.8
  collect 8443 quest 3161.1 @38.3,61.9

step Thistleshrub Valley
  tip West of the compound the cactus creatures fill the valley; only the Dew Collectors carry a dew gland. Most mobs in Tanaris can drop OOX-17/TN's distress beacon, rarely: keep it if you see one.
  kill 5490 quest 3362.1
  kill 5485 quest 3362.2
  collect 8428 quest 2605.1 @29.2,66.1
  collect 8623 optional                 -- OOX-17/TN Distress Beacon, a rare drop

step Tooga's escort
  tip Tooga waits in the valley. Walk him all the way to his wife Torta in Steamwheedle Port, north-east across the desert: stay close, slow down for him and fight off what attacks him. Do not mount or hearth out of his reach. Yeh'kinya stands in the port too.
  accept 1560                           -- Tooga
  complete 1560
  turnin 1560                           -- Torta, Steamwheedle Port
  turnin 3520                           -- Yeh'kinya

step Gadgetzan
  tip Ride south-west to Gadgetzan.
  turnin 2781                           -- Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle
  turnin 2605                           -- Marin Noggenfogger
  accept 2606
  turnin 2606                           -- Sprinkle
  accept 2641                           -- the Violet Tragan grows in the Hinterlands, around level 48
  turnin 3362                           -- Tran'rek
  turnin 82                             -- Alchemist Pestlezugg
  accept 10                             -- Senior Surveyor Fizzledowser
  turnin 5863                           -- Andi Lynn

step Marvon Rivetseeker
  tip South down the road again.
  turnin 3161

step Scrimshank's gear
  tip Further south, Junior Surveyor Scrimshank's gear lies at the mouth of a Centipaar hive.
  collect 8593 quest 10.1 @56.0,71.2

step OOX-17/TN
  tip Only with the distress beacon: OOX-17/TN sits south-east of Scrimshank's hive. Escort it north to Steamwheedle Port; its reward waits with Oglethorpe in Booty Bay.
  accept 351 optional
  turnin 351 optional                   -- Homing Robot OOX-17/TN
  accept 648 optional
  complete 648 optional

step Gadgetzan
  hearth "Gadgetzan"
  turnin 10                             -- Senior Surveyor Fizzledowser
  accept 110
  turnin 110                            -- Alchemist Pestlezugg
  accept 113
  turnin 113                            -- Senior Surveyor Fizzledowser
  accept 32                             -- for Zilzibin Drumlore in Orgrimmar, around level 50

step Orgrimmar
  only Hunter,Shaman
  zone Orgrimmar
  tip Fly to Orgrimmar and train: the next guide's training stop is the Undercity, which has no Hunter or Shaman trainer. Then fly to Ratchet.
  fly "Orgrimmar"
  train class

step Thunder Bluff
  only Druid
  zone Thunder Bluff
  tip Fly to Thunder Bluff and train with Turak Runetotem on Elder Rise, then fly to Ratchet.
  fly "Thunder Bluff"
  train class

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- To the Searing Gorge

step Fly to Ratchet
  fly "Ratchet"

step Boat to Booty Bay
  zone The Barrens
  tip The boat to Booty Bay docks at Ratchet's pier, below the flight master's hill.
  goto 63.4,38.5 "Ratchet pier"

step Fly to Kargath
  zone Stranglethorn Vale
  tip From the Booty Bay flight master, above the harbour.
  fly "Kargath"

step The Grimesilt Dig Site
  zone Searing Gorge
  tip Take the pass out of Kargath's west side into the Searing Gorge, then ride south-west to the dig site. The Wooden Outhouse stands at its southern end; the Dark Iron Geologists dig just north of it. Bring 15 Silk Cloth (the Auction House sells it).
  accept 4449 object 173265             -- the Wooden Outhouse
  kill 5839 quest 4449.1
  collect 4306 quest 4449.2
  turnin 4449 object 173265

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Thorium Point and Kalaran

step Thorium Point
  tip Ride north-west across the gorge; Thorium Point is the scaffolded camp in the north-west.
  getfp "Thorium Point" npc 3305        -- Grisha
  accept 7728 object 179827             -- The Wanted/Missing/Lost & Found board
  accept 7729 object 179827
  accept 7723                           -- Hansel Heavyhands
  accept 7724
  accept 7727
  accept 7722                           -- Master Smith Burninate

step Kalaran Windblade
  tip Kalaran stands alone south of Thorium Point, at the edge of the Cauldron. Listen to his story.
  accept 3441
  turnin 3441
  accept 3442

step The Cauldron
  tip Heavy War Golems patrol the Cauldron below Kalaran and drop the oil; the Magma and Blazing Elementals drifting among them drop the hearts. The Dark Iron Taskmasters and Slavers drive the slaves on the paths; a Slaver may drop the Grimesilt Outhouse Key: keep it.
  kill 5854 quest 7723.1
  collect 10511 quest 3442.2
  collect 10509 quest 3442.1
  kill 5846 quest 7729.1
  kill 5844 quest 7729.2
  collect 11818 optional                -- Grimesilt Outhouse Key, a rare drop

step Kalaran Windblade
  turnin 3442
  accept 3443

step The Steamsmiths' furnaces
  tip The Dark Iron Steamsmiths work the furnaces in the middle of the Cauldron; half of them carry a Thorium Plated Dagger, one in ten the Smithing Tuyere. Slaves, Slavers and Taskmasters carry daggers too.
  collect 10551 quest 3443.1
  collect 18959 quest 7728.1

step Kalaran Windblade
  turnin 3443
  note His next request needs the Symbol of Ragnaros from elite cultists: leave it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- The rest of the gorge

step The Slag Pit
  tip The Slag Pit opens in the north of the Cauldron. Incendosaurs swim in its lava pools: pull them to the edge. The secret plans lie on the pit's upper ledge.
  kill 9318 quest 7727.1
  collect 18922 quest 7722.1 @40.5,35.7

step Greater Lava Spiders
  tip The Greater Lava Spiders roam the plateaus and lava pools in the south-west of the gorge.
  kill 5858 quest 7724.1

step Dark Iron Lookouts
  tip The Dark Iron Lookouts stand on the ridges around the sentry towers south of the Cauldron; about one in ten carries the Lookout's Spyglass.
  collect 18960 quest 7728.2

step The Key to Freedom
  tip Only with the Grimesilt Outhouse Key: back east to the Wooden Outhouse at the dig site.
  accept 4451 optional
  turnin 4451 optional object 173265

step Thorium Point
  tip Ride back north to Thorium Point. Stay here: the next guide starts with the flight to Stonard.
  turnin 7723                           -- Hansel Heavyhands
  turnin 7724
  turnin 7727
  turnin 7728                           -- Taskmaster Scrange
  turnin 7729
  turnin 7722                           -- Master Smith Burninate
